        ["Portfolio.BeyondAcademics.Culture.Year2.CriticalThinking.P1.Text"] = "Critical thinking is a set of methods to think better: analyze, question, or distrust your own opinions—in other words, be better prepared to deal with speeches or life situations that everyone encounters daily. It also helps us become smarter together and better resist ideologies or nonsense of all kinds that poison the public space. (Source: ",
        ["Portfolio.BeyondAcademics.Culture.Year2.CriticalThinking.P1.Link"] = "KissKissBankBank",
        ["Portfolio.BeyondAcademics.Culture.Year2.CriticalThinking.P2"] = "This course sometimes uses political examples from current events. It is politically neutral and focuses solely on respect and critical thinking, not on opinions or ideologies. I am following this “Cogito” course to strengthen my critical thinking and improve my ability to step back, analyze, and question what I read online and hear in real life.",
        ["Portfolio.BeyondAcademics.Culture.Year2.CriticalThinking.Img"] = "Cogito course",
        ["Portfolio.BeyondAcademics.Culture.Year2.Travels.Title"] = "Travels in European countries",
        ["Portfolio.BeyondAcademics.Culture.Year2.Travels.Intro"] = "In August 2024, I took a one-week solo trip across the capitals of three countries:",
        ["Portfolio.BeyondAcademics.Culture.Year2.Travels.List1"] = "Belgium (Brussels)",
        ["Portfolio.BeyondAcademics.Culture.Year2.Travels.List2"] = "Luxembourg (Luxembourg)",
        ["Portfolio.BeyondAcademics.Culture.Year2.Travels.List3"] = "The Netherlands (Amsterdam)",
        ["Portfolio.BeyondAcademics.Culture.Year2.Travels.P1"] = "In Brussels, I visited the Royal Museums of Fine Arts (paintings, sculptures, and drawings + René Magritte exhibition), Autoworld (vintage car museum), the Atomium, and the European Quarter.",
        ["Portfolio.BeyondAcademics.Culture.Year2.Travels.P2"] = "In Luxembourg, I was able to see the Adolphe Bridge and the Bourbon Plateau.",
        ["Portfolio.BeyondAcademics.Culture.Year2.Travels.Link"] = "See my travels page",
        ["Portfolio.BeyondAcademics.Culture.Year2.EcritPlus.P1"] = "Ecrit+ is an online platform to practice the French language in different areas: spelling, grammar, conjugation, vocabulary, etc. Last year I got a score of 200, and I set myself the goal of reaching a score of 300 by improving my level in all the available skills.",

        ["Portfolio.BeyondAcademics.Culture.Year2.S4.Title"] = "Semester 4",
        ["Portfolio.BeyondAcademics.Culture.Year2.S4.Intro"] = "For this semester, I chose a single objective: reading The Chronicles of Narnia in English. I don’t read much and I’ve never had strong motivation to read. That’s why exploring Irish culture while practicing my English at the same time seemed like a good idea.",
        ["Portfolio.BeyondAcademics.Culture.Year2.S4.Method.Title"] = "Method:",
        ["Portfolio.BeyondAcademics.Culture.Year2.S4.Method.P1"] = "I forced myself to read at least 15 pages a day until it became a habit. This experience didn’t make me love reading, but what I found fun—and what made me succeed—was the challenge of reading in English. I had never read a book in English before, and I consider my English level to be average. Since it was difficult to understand everything, it became a personal challenge. I ended up enjoying spending time reading in English and, above all, learning new words and expressions.",
        ["Portfolio.BeyondAcademics.Culture.Year2.S4.Method.P2"] = "I wrote down all the words and their translations. Here are my favorite words I discovered:",
